          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Dry cough for approximately 7 days, worse in the evening and when supine; no sputum or haemoptysis."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-2",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Associated and denied respiratory symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mild increased fatigue. Denies shortness of breath at rest, wheeze, chest pain, pleuritic pain, chest tightness, fever, rigors, and productive sputum. No history of recurrent pneumonia."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-3",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-3",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Nasal and throat symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Nasal dryness and nocturnal throat tickle. Possible air-conditioning or new laundry powder irritation; these are not confirmed."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-4",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-4",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Other reported symptoms and status"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Oral intake is okay; still mobilising with baseline four-wheeled walker. Denies orthopnoea, paroxysmal nocturnal dyspnoea, and noticed weight gain. Leg oedema is about the same as usual; nocturia unchanged."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-5",
